wajo18_q8.solution:
Let the legs of the right-angle triangle be \(2 x\) and \(2 y\). Then we are given that<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
&amp; x^{2}+(2 y)^{2}=22^{2} \\
&amp; (2 x)^{2}+y^{2}=31^{2}
\end{aligned}
$$<br>and we need to find \(\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}+(2 y)^{2}}\). Adding the two equations, we have<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
5 x^{2}+5 y^{2} &amp; =22^{2}+31^{2} \\
4 x^{2}+4 y^{2} &amp; =\frac{4}{5}\left(22^{2}+31^{2}\right) \\
&amp; =\frac{4}{5}(484+961) \\
&amp; =\frac{4}{5} \cdot 1445 \\
&amp; =4 \cdot 289 \\
&amp; =2^{2} \cdot 17^{2} \\
\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}+(2 y)^{2}} &amp; =2 \cdot 17=34.
\end{aligned}
$$
